WEBVTT

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.020
Fifteen years ago,

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.850
the former Duke Bleichröder 
led an expedition

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:13.030
into the Enchanted Forest in search

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:15.320
of a magical panacea,

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.020
<i>This makes me nostalgic...</i>

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:19.430
but it couldn't have ended worse, 
leaving 2,000 soldiers

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.420
<i>This watered-down tea.</i>

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:22.120
and the former duke dead.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:27.660
We responded to the former duke's request 
and dispatched our army, as well,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.560
but the leader and everyone else...

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:37.090
The corpses of all those fallen have now 
become undead, specifically zombies.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:43.770
This is why our Lord has requested that we 
purify all the undead before they can become

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:46.730
greater undead, like liches.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.190
He's asking us to send troops again?

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.580
Who's that guy with the bad attitude?

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:57.880
They just mentioned it, remember?

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:00.580
That's Well's eldest brother, Kurt.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:03.700
That one's the second brother, Hermann,

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:07.000
and if I remember right, the one 
behind them is a village chief

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.040
who's a close aide to their father.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.230
We'll be handling the task of purification.

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:13.940
The reason we paid you a visit

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:17.830
was to discuss how to handle the monsters 
we'll defeat during that process.

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:20.100
The Enchanted Forest is our domain!

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.660
So it's standard for you to pay tribute

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:27.040
after converting any raw materials from 
the monsters defeated there into coin!

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.340
Yes, and we intend to do so.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:35.110
Which is why we're here to 
negotiate the rate of tribute.

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:38.490
Klaus, how much is standard?

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:41.780
I'd say... roughly thirty percent.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:44.290
Fifty percent, then.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:48.680
If you can't pay it, then give up and leave.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:52.650
And what will you do with the arms 
and armor of the purified soldiers?

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:56.220
We intend to recover as many of 
their personal effects as possible.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.180
I see.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:00.360
Hear that, Brother?

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.510
They're willing to retrieve 
our people's belongings.

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.460
Let's be reasonable.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:07.890
There's no need to recover their belongings.

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:09.900
What are you saying?

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:13.120
All of our soldiers are poor.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:15.690
None of them possess any 
items worth anything.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:18.360
So retrieving them isn't necessary.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.140
This guy...

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.780
Besides, their funerals have already been held.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.740
Pardon me,

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:29.330
but unless funerals are conducted 
after the souls have been purified,

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.590
they won't give the dead true peace.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:39.700
I would be happy to help conduct the 
funerals again after purification.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:43.060
Could you please back down, "Saint"?

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:45.640
We're impoverished nobles.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:50.600
You're after the gratuities due 
when performing a funeral, right?

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:55.070
Hey! Would you cut it out already?

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:59.980
Wendelin, you might be the heroic 
Dragon Slayer or whatever now,

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:02.140
but are all your men ruffians, as well?

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:04.370
Th-This jerk...

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:08.110
I sincerely appreciate your valuable opinion!

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:10.430
I will be sure to keep it in mind.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:16.750
Now, shall we begin the official 
negotiations, Sir Baumeister?

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:17.950
How dare you?!

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:20.970
Are you suggesting any discussion 
with me isn't official?!

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:25.270
We are here to negotiate with 
the lord, Sir Baumeister.

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:29.440
Furthermore, you should be 
more considerate of your tone.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:32.960
Even if this man is your younger brother,
 he's still a baron.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:36.700
You dare speak to me like 
that as mere retainers?!

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:40.610
I'm hungry.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.530
<i>For whatever reason,</i>

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:48.220
<i>my brother's turned into a toxic client.</i>

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:18.110
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:18.110
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:18.110
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:18.110
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:18.110
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:18.110
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:18.110
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:18.110
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:24.970
Episode 10
Toxic? Are You Kidding Me?!

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:27.630
What was the head auditor thinking, 
sending me such an injudicious letter?!

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:31.120
Now, let's begin the village meeting.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.560
Um, before we start,

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:37.230
I've heard that Sir Wendelin has 
returned to purify our sons

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:41.020
who were left behind in the forest.

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:47.400
What of it?

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:51.110
Listen! That man has not returned home!

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:54.980
He is only here as an adventurer 
fulfilling a quest!

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:58.370
Once he finishes purifying them, 
he will leave this land once more!

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:01.340
Isn't that right, Sir Kurt?

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:08.970
Has he always hated me that much?

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:13.430
It was after you left home 
that he lost all reason.

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:15.500
He's constantly been on edge,

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:18.410
afraid the heroic Dragon Slayer
would steal his position

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:19.980
as heir to the knightdom.

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:23.360
But I'd never do that to him.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.320
All right, everyone,

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:27.530
thank you for waiting!

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:31.070
Marlene!

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:39.770
Darling, pour Brantag a drink.

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:41.440
Oh, sorry.

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:43.210
Here, have some.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:45.840
This is mead made here on our land.

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:50.280
No, I'll pass on liquor tonight.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:52.750
What? That's unusual!

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:55.510
You're usually drowning in 
liquor from dawn to dusk.

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:58.020
That's an exaggeration.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:02.120
Darling, offer Well some pie.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:03.310
Oh, right, right.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:05.990
I wish you luck, Well.

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:10.740
I'm sure my own grandfather has become 
one of the undead in the forest, too.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:13.510
He was the head attendant, right?

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:16.290
He took good care of me when I was little.

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:19.250
I'll search for his belongings.

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:22.370
What a fine man you are!

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:24.670
Nothing like that imbecile!

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:28.690
Oh, if only you were the heir, Well!

00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:30.630
Hey, don't say that so loudly.

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.130
Who cares?

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:34.120
It's what everyone thinks!

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:38.280
I think we're about to get 
caught up in a succession crisis.

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:41.190
It looks like...

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:45.020
The best thing to do is 
finish up quickly and leave.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:08:00.170
All right, let's commence the operation 
to lure the zombies to us!

00:08:00.170 --> 00:08:01.370
One, two!

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:06.340
Hey! Soldiers of the Bleichröder Dukedom!

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:08.930
How could you let 2,000 men die?

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:11.300
Is your military incompetent?

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:13.570
No, no, they're worse than that.

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:16.010
Right, Dunce Dukedom?

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:19.030
You even brought my master down with you,

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:20.750
you useless commanders!

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:24.190
You're rotten and nasty!
You're rotten and nasty!

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:31.110
Um, will this really draw out the undead?

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:33.670
Yes, it'll lure them out.

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:36.070
They may not be all too smart,

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:39.600
but they still know when 
they're being insulted.

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:46.670
Here they come.

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:48.380
They're over here, too.

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:50.340
Now, Elise!

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:08.560
Now to expand the area of 
this purification spell!

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:20.330
Here come the zombies!

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:22.540
A huge march of zombies!

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:26.330
Okay, everyone keep your guard up!

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:27.460
Right!

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:41.430
We're not doing much.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:45.640
Come on. Retrieving their 
belongings is part of our job.

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:47.190
R-Right.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:57.260
Well, look!

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:59.350
I see one that looks like their boss!

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:00.700
Right there!

00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:04.160
Armor and weapons with 
prominent ornamentation...

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:05.730
There's no mistake.

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:07.870
That's the general commander of this army,

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:10.820
the former Duke Bleichröder.

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:14.300
All done with the boss!

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:17.260
Huh? Are we finished now?

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:20.290
No, there's still that woman's grandfather.

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:23.170
Right, I don't think we've seen the armor

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:25.800
Marlene said her grandfather was wearing.

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:34.480
Her grandfather?

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:43.820
A wyvern.

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:48.020
It's turned undead, too.

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:52.540
Huh? Then why isn't it being 
purified by the holy magic?

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:12.770
The magic is working on it.

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:17.110
But unlike the zombies, 
it'll take time to purify it.

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:20.570
Well, here come a lot of nasty-looking ones!

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:25.280
These must be the monsters the 
expedition killed fifteen years ago.

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:28.950
But regular soldiers could 
never defeat these things!

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:31.090
Alfred was with them.

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:32.880
That's my master for you.

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:40.220
All right, keep your guards up this time!

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:41.550
Right!

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:05.660
Well, look.

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:08.410
That armor...

00:12:09.230 --> 00:12:10.750
It's probably her grandfather.

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:21.910
My granddaughter?

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:24.590
It spoke!

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:27.800
Tsk! It's turned into a damn lich.

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:30.390
She has her husband under her thumb,

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:32.020
and she's living a good life.

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:34.020
I see.

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:50.270
Take care of her.

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:09.510
Honestly, thank you so much.

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:12.740
Now my son can finally rest in peace.

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:15.190
Listen up, everyone!

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:18.150
Sir Kurt has a message for you!

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:21.610
Listen to me. Once the services are over,

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:24.460
you are to hand all of the rusted armor

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:27.610
and broken swords over to 
our blacksmith, Eckhart!

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:29.320
What? No way!

00:13:31.380 --> 00:13:36.690
U-Um, Sir Kurt, we have no 
bodies to bury for our dead,

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:39.560
so we hoped to bury those in their stead.

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:40.920
What nonsense.

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:43.880
Our territory lacks enough iron.

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:48.840
We'll be reusing those 
arms to develop this land.

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:52.580
That's what the dead would 
truly want, is it not?

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:55.270
But that's cruel.

00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:58.730
Once the services are done, 
turn them over at once!

00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:00.120
Sir Kurt...

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:03.150
What, Wendelin?

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:05.780
I understand you're short on resources,

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:07.360
but you don't have to take their things.

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:12.830
Do I hear a lowly adventurer 
questioning me, the lord heir?

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:14.680
Then if you had iron,

00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:16.790
you wouldn't need to take away their things?

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:18.300
Of course.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:19.710
In that case...

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:24.170
I present you with this.

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:29.160
Now there's no need to take away 
the dead men's belongings, right?

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:31.800
Wendelin...

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:35.580
What shall we do, Sir Kurt?

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:37.240
Leave him be.

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:39.770
He's done with his purification.

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:42.170
He'll be leaving this land soon enough.

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:43.960
We just have to be patient until then.

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:49.200
Thank you so much, Sir Wendelin!

00:14:54.730 --> 00:14:56.090
You've done well.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:15:00.710
Now we will begin the task 
of identifying their owners.

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:03.590
We will notify you once 
our assessment is complete.

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:08.050
Mission complete. Now I can 
bid farewell to my old home.

00:15:08.310 --> 00:15:13.490
Now, I would like you to remain on 
standby in the Baumeister Knightdom.

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:14.010
Huh?

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:17.110
I'll write a letter to Sir Baumeister myself

00:15:17.110 --> 00:15:21.480
so you can go hunting in the Enchanted 
Forest and other undeveloped lands.

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:25.440
Um, if possible, I would prefer to 
be stationed anywhere but my home.

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:28.680
Come on, what's wrong with 
staying there a while?

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:29.350
Huh?

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:32.160
Their mead is superb!

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:35.620
You never drank any, Brantag.

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:44.360
All goes as planned?

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:46.740
Yes.

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:57.470
Oh, Sir Wendelin.

00:15:57.760 --> 00:15:59.960
I thought you had left already.

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:02.190
That was our plan,

00:16:02.610 --> 00:16:07.480
but we were ordered to remain here until 
they identified the owners of those items.

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:08.440
Oh?

00:16:08.770 --> 00:16:13.200
But identifying the belongings of 
2,000 dead won't be easy, will it?

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:15.150
They all look the same, too,

00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:16.910
so it'll take some time.

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:18.840
I see.

00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:25.880
In that case, would you like to participate 
in the funerals being held tomorrow?

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:27.600
Funerals?

00:16:32.110 --> 00:16:34.850
Now, let us offer up our prayers.

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:46.190
We're so lucky to have the 
Saint offer prayers for us.

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:48.650
Why is Elise doing this?

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:51.610
Because the priest here
is getting old, Klaus said.

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:59.740
I can't believe Sir Kurt wouldn't come.

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:18.620
Sir Wendelin, please have 
some mead, if you'd like.

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:21.780
Oh, I'm good. Offer it to Brantag.

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:26.770
Actually, Sir Brantag refused, too.

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:27.500
Huh?

00:17:36.850 --> 00:17:39.070
Hey, that's...

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:41.390
The eldest brother's wife, right?

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:43.430
Yeah, that's my sister-in-law, Amalie.

00:17:46.610 --> 00:17:48.620
Now, let's pray.

00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:49.460
Okay.

00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:02.740
I'm sorry for not paying you a proper visit.

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:05.570
You've been quite busy, Well.

00:18:05.570 --> 00:18:08.560
Oh, pardon me. I spoke out of old habit.

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:12.820
You're a baron now, so I must be more polite.

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:16.530
Oh, I don't mind. This isn't 
a formal setting, anyway.

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:19.990
Wow, it really is the heroic Dragon Slayer!

00:18:20.340 --> 00:18:24.450
Hey, please tell us about the time you 
defeated that defeated that bone dragon!

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:29.370
I can't believe it's a bone dragon!

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:31.840
What is it doing here?!

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:35.320
Bone, bone! Bone, bone, bone!

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:39.570
Damn! At this rate, 
the airship will be taken down!

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:39.630
Bone, bone, bone, bone!
 Bone, bone, bone, bone! Bone!

00:18:39.570 --> 00:18:43.490
Um, Brantag, if you'd like, he...

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:43.390
Bone, bone, bone, bone, bone!
 Bone, bone, bone, bone! Bone!

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:46.770
Bone! Bone! Bone! Bone!

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:46.790
I mean, I could blast it with holy magic?

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:47.850
Bone!

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:51.110
Come on! You're the main character, 
so put some more spirit into it!

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:52.770
Oh, bone! Bone, bone! Bone! Bone!

00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:52.410
But...

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:56.780
Bone! If you don't attack me,
I'm gonna attack you, bone!

00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:56.000
Why am I playing Well in the first place?

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:58.740
Would you rather play Brantag, then?

00:18:57.280 --> 00:19:00.530
Is that what you want, bone?
A-Are you sure, bone?!

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:00.740
I'll stick with Well.

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:02.700
Bone, bone!

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:06.450
Bone! Bone, bone! Bone, bone!

00:19:02.930 --> 00:19:07.100
Hey, boy, do something with your magic!

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:10.760
Bone! Bone, bone... bone...

00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:11.920
Uh, first I fly...

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:11.920
More spirit!

00:19:14.190 --> 00:19:17.450
Your kids have really grown.

00:19:17.890 --> 00:19:20.840
Yes, and I've gotten older, too.

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:24.300
Those children are all I ever think about.

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:27.380
I hope they can always get along as brothers.

00:19:28.630 --> 00:19:30.690
Hey! Are we gonna get some candy?

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:33.480
Hey, this isn't a festival.

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:36.440
Okay, leave this one to your uncle.

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:37.480
Ta-da!

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:39.860
Stir, stir, stir...

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:41.280
Okay, here you go.

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:42.520
What is it?

00:19:42.520 --> 00:19:44.610
It's mizuame. Try it.

00:19:44.610 --> 00:19:46.420
Um, okay...

00:19:46.420 --> 00:19:47.860
Thank you.

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:52.290
It's good!

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:53.720
Hey.

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:56.210
Me, too. Me, too!

00:19:56.530 --> 00:19:58.170
Mizuame for me, too!

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:03.010
Stir, stir, stir...

00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:07.870
Bye-bye!

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:14.890
Sir Wendelin...

00:20:18.930 --> 00:20:20.660
I have a request.

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:26.280
Would you please become 
the heir of this territory?

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:27.500
What?

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:31.460
I'm sure you've at least vaguely realized

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:34.460
that this is what the people here desire.

00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:36.920
Wait, wait... Wh-What brought this on?

00:20:37.310 --> 00:20:40.630
This land has no future under Sir Kurt.

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:42.890
Um, a-at any rate,

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:46.090
you shouldn't let my father or 
older brother hear about this.

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:47.360
I don't care if they do.

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:50.100
I've already made my peace.

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:54.160
But I still want to live as an adventurer,

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:56.400
so owning territory would just be...

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:59.110
So long as you leave someone 
you trust in charge of the land,

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:01.330
you should be able to continue your adventures.

00:21:01.330 --> 00:21:05.070
I've heard you already have a retainer 
with talent for such things.

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:10.030
You mean Roderich? 
Where did you learn about him?

00:21:10.260 --> 00:21:12.240
If you decide to do so,

00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:15.000
then you will have my support, too.

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:15.970
Wait.

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:20.290
I've already been made the head 
of a different, independent line.

00:21:20.290 --> 00:21:24.970
So the royal palace would never 
allow me to inherit this territory.

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:29.600
Those at the royal palace aren't 
concerned with such formalities.

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:32.220
What makes you say that?

00:21:32.610 --> 00:21:36.440
This is something they desire, too.

00:21:37.270 --> 00:21:38.400
The palace?

00:21:38.620 --> 00:21:40.400
You're very clever.

00:21:44.260 --> 00:21:48.780
I'm surprised a man from these outskirts could
 reach that conclusion from conjecture alone.

00:21:49.100 --> 00:21:51.960
I'm honored by your compliment.

00:21:52.340 --> 00:21:56.000
Brantag, what on earth is going on here?

00:21:56.270 --> 00:21:58.460
It's exactly as he just said.

00:21:59.110 --> 00:22:04.130
Those at the palace want you to 
become the lord of this territory.
